# --- Project-specific ---
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
checkpoints/*
!checkpoints/.gitkeep
runs/*
!runs/.gitkeep
!outputs/.gitkeep
# Contents, not the directory itself. `experiments/*/outputs/` excluded the DIRECTORY, and git
# does not descend into an excluded directory, so no `!` rule underneath could ever match. The
# .gitkeep negation below had silently never worked. Trailing /* is what makes negation possible.
experiments/*/outputs/*
!experiments/*/outputs/.gitkeep
# Variant output dirs (e.g. outputs_instrumented/ from a re-run that must not overwrite
# the original records). Without this they are untracked-but-not-ignored, which is exactly
# what a stray `git add -A` sweeps into an unrelated commit.
experiments/*/outputs_*/
wandb/
*.pt
# EXP-036 head checkpoints ARE tracked. A trained policy head is a Linear(64 -> 6), 390
# parameters, about 1.6 KB, so all 48 runs of a sweep cost roughly 75 KB. Versioning them is
# what makes "never retrain to re-evaluate" true from a fresh checkout rather than only true
# on whichever machine happens to still hold the run. Must come after `*.pt`: last match wins.
!experiments/*/outputs/*_head.pt
# EXP-047 FINE-TUNED encoders are tracked for the same reason, at a different price. Each is a
# SensoryCortex (144 -> 128 -> 64), 26,816 parameters, about 108 KB, so the 18 runs of the
# experiment cost roughly 2 MB. Claim 2 re-probes these weights, and regenerating one costs
# ~5.6 core-hours; the whole set is a ~12 h laptop run.
#
# The PRETRAINED encoders (`exp040_encoder_s*.pt`) used to be excluded here, on the ground that
# they are "reproducible from EXP-040's phase 1". MEASURED 2026-09-22, that ground is FALSE off
# the machine that made them:
#
#   laptop, where the originals were made : 12 of 12 byte-identical  (deterministic)
#   this VPS, a different x86 machine     :  0 of 2 byte-identical  (NOT portable)
#
# And the difference is not last-bit float noise. Only 7.1% of the 26,824 parameters match,
# max|delta| is 2.38, and the cosine between original and regenerated is 0.77 - a substantially
# different network. FIFTEEN experiments load these encoders frozen (EXP-041 through EXP-066),
# so a fresh clone on any other machine reproduces none of their published numbers.
#
# The regenerated encoder is a VALID encoder, just not THE encoder: its move-accuracy 0.4346
# sits inside the seed spread 0.4300-0.4373. So the FINDINGS are likely reproducible while the
# NUMBERS are not, and only tracking the artifacts makes the stronger claim true.
# 2.8 MB for all 24. See experiments/040_pretrained_encoder_policy/verify_regeneration.py.
!experiments/*/outputs/*_encoder.pt
!experiments/*/outputs/exp040_encoder_s*.pt
*.pth
results.csv
training_curves.png

